# Features

Mistake without this: put step defs here, fake mark simulate, ship non-published paths, or use `@full` / shipping vocabulary in Gherkin.

**Docs:** `docs/vocabulary.md` · `docs/scenario-policy.md` · Bugbot: [BUGBOT.md](../BUGBOT.md)

```text
porto-data (facts) → porto-features (BDD contracts) → implementor step defs (outside)
```

Wire Examples / `orders.generated.yaml`: regenerate via Lab `matrix-orders-sync.py` — do not hand-edit.

1. Gherkin is implementation-agnostic (no SDK class/module names).
2. Given/When letter input = weight (+ optional envelope or product id); service input = `kind`; Then may assert catalog `id` or feature `kind`.
3. No `tests/bdd/steps/**` or runner glue in this repo.
4. Published only: `porto_features/errors.json`, `features/`, `fixtures/`. No `contracts/` or package `matrix/`.
5. Feature tags: `@sdk` or `@adapters`; paid: `@canary` / `@heavy` (never `@full` / `@release`). All tags lowercase.
6. Offline: `When I resolve the letter`. Paid: `When I create a mark`. No `mark_simulate` / stamp simulate.
7. Letter / price / mailing — not shipping / shipment. No `When I check restrictions`.

Before merge: `make quality` · `make test-cov` · update vocabulary/CHANGELOG when contracts change.
